Wait, fsevents.js does `require("./fsevents.node")`. Node resolves directory `fsevents.node/index.js`. But will Node treat a directory with `.node` in name fine? Yes, directory resolution ignores extension. Good.

But there's a catch: Node's require for a path ending in `.node` — the LOAD_AS_FILE step tries `X`, `X.js`, `X.json`, `X.node`. It tries `fsevents.node` as file first. There is no file, then `fsevents.node.js`? no. Then `fsevents.node.json`? no. Then `fsevents.node.node`? no. Then LOAD_AS_DIRECTORY: `fsevents.node/package.json` (none) then `fsevents.node/index.js` → yes! Good.

